Gemini:
The wind beats, shouting down through the valleys from the mountains;
A woman stands, looking down at the river, on a cliff, with her hair spread;
She reminds me of a light-deprived star with pale, trembling lips.
She makes no sound… startled she trembles, as she gazes down at the river;
How dreadfully it roars, how dreadfully it flows!
Grimacing and cruel, the black valley rages,
“Do not kill yourself!” if only one would advise her so.
The woman closed her eyes, and quickly plunged into the whirlpool.

