Gemini:
I. The Khevsurians were at the guest-house, beer brewed in the cauldron;
They sat upon the flat roofs and feasted, drinking it from bowls;
Some played the panduri, singing loudly to its tune,
Laying heroic tales as a bridge to the listeners' feelings;
With fervor, they recited the sacred names of heroes in verse;
The elders smoked their pipes, smoke wrapped around them like mist,
They recounted their deeds, offering blessings for the heroes.
To instruct the young, they remembered them with praise:
"It is for you to show, who among you shall prove to be a man from this day forth!"

